# Website Starter — Architecture & Implementation Plan

## Overview

`website-starter` is a Zavcode **package** (product) that provides a ready-to-use content website built on Payload CMS + Next.js. It includes a full content model (Pages, Media, Users), layout blocks (hero, page-content, forms), i18n, SEO, seeds, schemas, hooks, services, and app route templates.

The package is assembled with a theme from `/ui/themes` and optional plugins into a standalone ZIP repo — structurally identical to `dev-playground`.

## Goals

- Provide a production-ready website base that can be assembled into a standalone app via the build script.
- Keep the content model, schemas, hooks, and routes **in the package** — not in the app runtime.
- Maintain full type safety during development via package-level `payload-types.ts` generation.
- Decouple presentation (themes) from content model (package) via the page builder adapter pattern.

## Non-Goals

- No ecommerce features (orders, products, checkout, VAT, Stripe) — that's `ecommerce-starter`.
- No user dashboard / private area — that's ecommerce-specific.

---

## Three Type Domains

This is the most important architectural decision. Types are split across three domains with clear boundaries.

| Domain            | Where types live                           | Who owns them                           | Example                                        |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| **Payload types** | `payload-types.ts` — generated per-package | Package (collections define the shape)  | `import { Page } from '@/payload-types'`       |
| **Theme props**   | Hand-written interfaces in `ui/themes/`    | Theme (generic, no Payload dependency)  | `export interface HeroProps { title: string }` |
| **Plugin types**  | `import type { Config } from 'payload'`    | Plugin (standalone, no `payload-types`) | `import type { PluginConfig } from './types'`  |

### Bridge: Page Builder / Adapter

The **layout builder engine** lives in **`utils/layout-builder`** (shared lib). It is generic: it accepts **types + section map** and renders blocks. Packages (website-starter, ecommerce-starter) depend on it and pass their own `PageSection` type and `sectionComponents` map. This keeps a single implementation and consistent behaviour (keying, unknown-type warning, etc.) while each package stays type-safe with its own Payload types. See [Layout Builder (utils)](#layout-builder-utils-layout-builder) and `.cursor/rules/feature/layout-builder.mdc`.

