## Key Architectural Decisions

- **Package generates its own `payload-types.ts`** from its own collections. This gives full type safety during development without needing the assembled app.
- **`@/*` path alias** in the package's `tsconfig.json` points to `./src/*`. The same alias in the assembled app also points to `./src/*`. All imports survive assembly unchanged.
- **Theme components never import from `payload-types`**. They define their own generic props. The page builder in the package is the adapter between the two type domains.
- **Plugins are additive**. They don't break package schemas because schemas only validate package-owned data. Plugin-specific types are internal to each plugin.
- **Pages collection** (new) is the centerpiece — it has a `layout` field (array of blocks) that drives the page builder.
- **Runtime** loads the package set in `ZAVCODE_PACKAGE`; use `pnpm dev:runtime` to run the app with that package.
- **Layout builder** lives in `utils/layout-builder`; packages pass their types + section map into it for reuse and single-place maintenance.
- **Query building** (params schema, validation, api-fetch) lives in **`utils/query-builder`** (`@zavcode/query-builder`); all packages depend on it instead of duplicating (extract from dev-playground: `schemas/query-builder`, app `utils/query-builder`, `utils/api-fetch`).
- **Theme loading** (registry, active theme, theme provider) is a **reusable util** in `utils/`; the package does not ship its own theme folder, it uses this util (same behaviour as dev-playground `src/theme/`).
- **Payload config plugins** (SEO, form-builder) work the same way as in dev-playground: `payload/config/plugins/` with seo.ts, form-builder.ts, index.ts.
